          {
            "_key": "avc",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "One grape, two terroirs"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "h2"
      },
      {
        "_key": "avl",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "ave",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "In the "
          },
          {
            "_key": "avg",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [
              "avf"
            ],
            "text": "Côte des Bar"
          },
          {
            "_key": "avh",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ", pinot noir dominates on Kimmeridgian marl. In "
          },
          {
            "_key": "avj",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [
              "avi"
            ],
            "text": "Montgueux"
          },
          {
            "_key": "avk",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ", it is chardonnay, on Turonian chalk. Soil, aspect and climate give each grape a different signature. The winemaker then blends the wines to find the balance of each cuvée; some are even made from a single grape."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [
          {
